# Review: GitHubPlugin

The polling sync, the push path and the pull-request review UI are solid. `syncRepoBinding` reads the repository
hourly, the organization daily, a conditional issue delta and one GraphQL batch for pull requests, then pushes
diverged fields through `pushRepoUpdates`; `sync-poll.test.ts` and `sync.test.ts` cover the delta, pull-request
mirroring, Repo description and issue title/status push, repo-rename and PR-status suppression. The review article
(Overview, Walkthrough and Files tabs, check runs, artifact pills, reviewed-file tracking) is covered by stories, and
the browser-extension import is covered end to end by two Playwright specs.

Gaps are in connection setup and discovery: nothing tests `onTokenCreated`, the App token's account naming, or
`GetGitHubRepositories` (sorting, `ghs_` installation repos). The organization success path (Organization and
member Persons) and `maxDaysBack` are untested.

Two divergences matter. Organizations are read once a day per binding (`membersReadAt` on the binding's snapshot),
not once per sync pass across bindings, so two repositories of one org each read it (F-3.4, T-8). And an
inaccessible repository records `GitHubRepoInaccessibleError` from `formatGitHubSyncFailure` as `lastError` and as
the error toast's text, not the spec's "Repository not accessible to integration token" (F-7.2, F-7.5).

Of 76 items: 35 done, 26 untested, 6 partial, 2 diverged, 7 missing.

